From 1a86ff08d39f1b19be75d857396962acfcc9defe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:14:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: the audio output of the display that Kodi uses,
 while the user has chosen none

Kodi's default audio output is the first one of the list, which on a PC is the analog output
of the sound chip of the board. With the TV on the HDMI output of the graphics card and a
sound bar on the TV's eARC, there was no sound until the output was found in Settings >
System > Audio (issue #6, 2026-10-25: an RTX 3090 with an LG C3).

The audio data of an HDMI or DisplayPort output (its ELD) names its display with the maker
and product codes and the name of the EDID that the graphics driver read. The windowing
system now says which display Kodi shows its picture on (KODI::UTILS::CDrivenDisplay, from
the EDID of its output), so the output of that display is known, not guessed. While a device
setting holds no choice of the user, the engine puts that output in it
(CActiveAE::ChooseOutputsForTheDisplay(), each time it loads its settings and when the
outputs change, as when the TV is turned on after Kodi started), for PCM and for passthrough.

- What is the user's choice: any change of the setting that neither the engine nor the list
  of the settings made (the list puts an output in a setting whose value is not among the
  outputs). Two hidden settings keep what was put there without the user
  (audiooutput.hadesautodevice, audiooutput.hadesautopassthroughdevice); a change by the user
  empties them, and the setting is never changed by this again. A value from an earlier
  version, where the list also put the first output there by itself, counts as the user's:
  what may be a choice is never changed. A reset to the default is a return to no choice.
- Fail-closed: with no output that has a display, with several of which none is known to be
  Kodi's (two TVs of one model), or when Kodi's display has no audio of its own (a monitor
  without speakers beside a TV), nothing changes and Kodi's default stays. Where Kodi's
  display is not known (another windowing system), only the one output with a display is
  taken.
- A rename of the same device by ValidateOutputDevices() keeps whose choice it is.
- The log says, without debugging, what was found and what was done.

Tested on the host: TestActiveAEFollowDisplay, with the EDIDs of the two displays of a
diagnostic of 2026-10-17 and an ELD built from one of them, which decodes to what ALSA read
of that display there (manufacture_id 0xa625, product_id 0x1); eight mutations of the rules
make it fail.
